[b]Where to find the uniques[/b] (each one opens with a vague tip, the exact location is a spoiler inside it)

[b]The lesser unique[/b]
[spoiler]

The lesser of uniques (barely a unique) is made of driftwood by someone with a lot of time on their hands and a habbit to watch over the ships in the sea.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MaxYari/Katars-KnucklesOpenMW/main/imgs/screenshots/driftwood_beaters_rocks.png[/img]

[b]Exact location (full spoiler)[/b]
[spoiler]

[b]Driftwood Beaters[/b]: on the bench at the top of the Seyda Neen lighthouse interior.

[/spoiler]

[/spoiler]

[b]The middle unique[/b]
[spoiler]

The middle of the uniques is of an arcane origin and as such is drawn to places of high magic. It also rather fancies inland lakes.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MaxYari/Katars-KnucklesOpenMW/main/imgs/screenshots/mage_fury_rocks.png[/img]

[b]Exact location (full spoiler)[/b]
[spoiler]

[b]Mage Fury[/b]: in the room with four pillars in Marandus, Upper Level, on the desk among a collection of scrolls and potions.

[/spoiler]

[/spoiler]

[b]The highest unique[/b]
[spoiler]

The highest of the three is of a dark and vicious nature, its kiss is poison and its owner schemes deep underground.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MaxYari/Katars-KnucklesOpenMW/main/imgs/screenshots/ebony_rose_hills.png[/img]

[b]Exact location (full spoiler)[/b]
[spoiler]

[b]Ebony Rose[/b]: Old Mournhold, Moril Manor, in the Dark Brotherhood hideout (the location where the local Brotherhood leader, Dandras Vules, resides). If [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/55064]Mercy: CAO[/url] is installed, Dandras himself will carry and use them; if not, the Ebony Rose katars can be found on a stool beside the fire, in the little corner where Dandras is found.

[/spoiler]

[/spoiler]

[/spoiler]

[size=5][b]Recommended mods[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/60362]The Combat Juice[/url], also by me - a layer of subtle "oomph" all over the combat, visual and audible, without touching any mechanics - every punch feels like it lands.
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/59205]Inventory Extender[/url] - shows the Hand to Hand type and the fatigue damage in weapon tooltips.
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/54950]QuickLoot[/url] - its loot tooltips show them too.
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/60361]Combat Sounds Overhaul Overhauled[/url], also by me - katars swing with a fist's whoosh and a blade's under it, knuckledusters with a fist's. Load [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/53859]Combat Sounds Overhaul[/url] above [font=Courier New]Katars&Knuckles.omwscripts[/font].
[/list]

[size=5][b]How to install[/b][/size]

[b]Requires OpenMW 0.51+[/b]

[list=1]
[*]Install the dependencies: [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/52596]ReAnimation[/url] (3.3 or
[/list]

newer) and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/60256]Max Yari's Script Services (MSS)[/url].

[list=1]
[*]Install this mod [b]with a mod organiser[/b]: download the archive and drag and drop it into your mod
[/list]

organiser of choice (e.g. [url=https://github.com/ModOrganizer2/modorganizer/releases]Mod Organizer 2[/url] on Windows or [url=https://github.com/grazelandsnomad/nerevarine_organizer/releases/tag/v0.70]Nerevarine Organizer[/url] on Linux). [b]Or[/b]: [url=https://modding-openmw.com/tips/installing-mods/]read this tutorial[/url] on how to install mods using the launcher or completely manually (it's also very easy). The archive has two folders: [font=Courier New]00 Core[/font] is the mod and [font=Courier New]01 Glass Glowset Patch[/font] is an optional patch (see Optional below). Mod organisers show an installer that explains them. If you install by hand, add [font=Courier New]00 Core[/font] as the data folder, and [font=Courier New]01 Glass Glowset Patch[/font] after it if you want it.

[list=1]
[*]Enable these in the "Content Files" tab of the OpenMW launcher, after [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/52596]ReAnimation[/url]:
[list]
[*][font=Courier New]Katars&Knuckles.omwaddon[/font] - needs Tribunal and Bloodmoon.
[*][font=Courier New]Katars&Knuckles_WorldPlacements.omwaddon[/font] - puts the rare weapons, and a few others, in the world. Needs Tribunal and Bloodmoon.
[*][font=Courier New]Katars&Knuckles_TamrielRebuilt.omwaddon[/font] - only if you are using [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/42145]Tamriel Rebuilt[/url], should be loaded after the Tamriel Rebuilt plugins: puts the weapons in Tamriel Rebuilt's levelled lists too. Requires [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/44537]Tamriel Data[/url].
[*][font=Courier New]Katars&Knuckles.omwscripts[/font]
[*][font=Courier New]Katars&Knuckles_Conjuration.omwscripts[/font] - adds the matching conjuration spell, Bound Fist, to some spell merchants.
[/list]
[*]OpenMW Launcher -> Settings -> Visuals -> Animations: "Use Additional Animation Sources" must be
[/list]

enabled.

[list=1]
[*]The weapons are added to the game's levelled lists - "levelled lists" are a thing that determines enemy/chest loot and merchant stock. Unfortunately, when multiple mods edit the same lists, the changes don't automatically sum up - only the last change wins. There is a solution to that though. If you use other mods that edit those lists too, merge your lists once your
[/list]

load order is set using one of the following utilities:

[list]
[*]Windows: [url=https://github.com/NullCascade/TES3Merge]TES3Merge[/url] or [url=https://gitlab.com/bmwinger/delta-plugin]DeltaPlugin[/url]
[*]Linux: [url=https://gitlab.com/bmwinger/delta-plugin]DeltaPlugin[/url]
[/list]
[list=1]
[*]If you have the launcher's "Factor Strength into Hand-to-Hand Combat" option on (Settings -> Gameplay),
[/list]

this mod provides the identical setting in Options -> Scripts -> Katars & Knuckles. You should turn it ON if you want stamina damage to remain consistent between bare-fist H2H and H2H weapons.

Optional:

[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/58693]Unofficial Tamriel Rebuilt Spells[/url] - Bound Fist then grows stronger with your Conjuration, following that mod's bound item settings (if you have the "Scale bound items" setting turned on in the Unofficial Tamriel Rebuilt Spells mod).
[*][b]PBR[/b]: the weapons come with PBR maps (normal and specular), so metal and crystal catch the light properly under [url=https://github.com/wareya/OpenMW-PBR/tree/0.51]Wareya's PBR shaders[/url]. They will probably look off with [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/53667]Rafael's Shader Pack[/url] PBR, but they should look fine without any PBR. PBR maps were made to match the overall vibes of [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/52114]Aesthetically Shiny Things[/url], which is also recommended. Launcher settings: "Auto Use Object Normal Maps" and "Auto Use Object Specular Maps" should be ON (launcher: Settings -> Visuals -> Shaders).
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/42762]Glass Glowset[/url]: tick "Glass Glowset Patch" in the installer (or add the [font=Courier New]01 Glass Glowset Patch[/font] folder after [font=Courier New]00 Core[/font]) and the glass katars fit its style - they glow like the rest of the glass set. Needs Glass Glowset installed.
[/list]

Have fun!

[size=5][b]Mod compatibility[/b][/size]

Probably compatible with mostly everything. If your mod needs to know whether a weapon is actually an H2H weapon or not (instead of the official short blade/blunt, as the engine sees them), there's a Lua API that can provide this information - see the "For modders" section below.

